      "writtenOn": "2023-08-29T17:45:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "print() already adds a final newline by default.\n\nThat said mixing print() supplied final newline with hardcoded `\\n` always feels slightly awkward, and the use of `output` string here is unnecessary.  That\u0027s not a new issue with this CL, but IMO might as well clean it up while you\u0027re at it.\n\nHow about:\n\n```\n        print(\"board:\", args.board)\n        print(\"channel:\", args.channel)\n        print(\"firmware:\", newvers)\n        print(\"firmware file:\", binfile)\n```\n\nNote the lack of a space after each colon is deliberate, print() adds that automatically by default when joining multiple args.",
